==== `build` says what it built (a fixed target, so the size is the same on every machine)
---- file one.azl
fn main() {
    print(1)
}
---- run build --target x86_64-linux one.azl
---- exit 0
---- stdout (empty)
---- stderr
built one (25 bytes of code)
---- exists one
==== `explain` with a code that is not one
---- run explain nonsense
---- exit 1
---- stdout (empty)
---- stderr
error: there is no error code 'nonsense'; `azol explain` lists them all
